{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And jackals will answer.</b> Plural form from איה (Leviticus 11:14):" "<b>And will answer.</b> Its meaning is a cry, or a dwelling, from the root מעון (Psalms 26:8):" "<b>In its widowhoods.</b> Some say its meaning is like בארמנותיו, like וידע אלמנותיו (Ezekiel 19:7), but it is not possible for a letter to interchange with another letter except for the letters alef, heh, vav, yod. And so its meaning is: each of the birds will answer there with its widowhoods:" "<b>And jackals.</b> Like אח הייתי לתנים (Job 30:29):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:41.401553534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}